sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client / Service<br/>(acts for user)
    participant EI as External IdP<br/>(Cognito user pool)
    participant AG as API Gateway<br/>/v1/token-exchange
    participant AZ as Lambda authorizer
    participant SSM as Parameter Store<br/>(client secrets)
    participant TX as TokenExchange<br/>Lambda
    participant SP as Service pool<br/>(Cognito)
    participant PT as PreTokenGeneration<br/>trigger
    participant DS as Downstream API

    Note over C,EI: Phase 1 — user authenticates (once)
    C->>EI: Authenticate user
    EI-->>C: User access token

    Note over C,SSM: Phase 2 — authorize the client
    C->>AG: POST token-exchange<br/>(Basic client creds, subject_token = user token)
    AG->>AZ: Validate client credentials
    AZ->>SSM: Get client secret (5-min cache)
    SSM-->>AZ: Secret
    AZ-->>AG: Allow (IAM policy)

    Note over AG,EI: Phase 3 — verify the user token
    AG->>TX: Invoke with user token
    TX->>EI: Fetch JWKS (aws-jwt-verify)
    EI-->>TX: JWKS
    alt signature / exp / aud invalid
        TX-->>C: 401 — fail closed (no token issued)
    end

    Note over TX,SP: Phase 4 — mint the delegated token
    TX->>SP: Custom auth flow<br/>(clientMetadata.OriginalUserToken)
    SP->>PT: Invoke PreTokenGeneration
    PT->>EI: Verify OriginalUserToken<br/>(clientMetadata is NOT validated by Cognito)
    EI-->>PT: Valid
    alt verification fails
        PT-->>SP: throw — fail closed (no token issued)
    end
    PT-->>SP: Add custom:original_* claims + service scopes
    SP-->>TX: Exchanged access token
    TX-->>C: RFC 8693 response<br/>(access_token, token_type, expires_in)

    Note over C,DS: Phase 5 — call downstream with least privilege
    C->>DS: Call with exchanged token<br/>(sub = service, custom:original_sub = user)
    DS-->>C: Response (per-user authz + full audit trail)
